{"question": "How should organizations handle identification and authentication of non-organizational users accessing federal systems?", "framework_version": "rev5", "answer_text": "Non-organizational users should be uniquely identified and authenticated. This includes accepting only NIST-compliant external authenticators and maintaining a list of accepted external authenticators.", "answer_text_with_citations": "Non-organizational users should be uniquely identified and authenticated. This includes accepting only NIST-compliant external authenticators and maintaining a list of accepted external authenticators.

Citations: ia-8_gdn, ia-8.2_gdn, ia-8.2_smt, ia-8.2_smt.a, ia-8.2_smt.b (NIST SP 800-53 Rev. 5)", "evidence_spans": [{"source_id": "ia-8_gdn", "span_text": "Non-organizational users include system users other than organizational users explicitly covered by [IA-2](#ia-2) . Non-organizational users are uniquely identified and authenticated for accesses other than those explicitly identified and documented in [AC-14](#ac-14) . Identification and authentication of non-organizational users accessing federal systems may be required to protect federal, proprietary, or privacy-related information (with exceptions noted for national security systems). Organizations consider many factors—including security, privacy, scalability, and practicality—when balancing the need to ensure ease of use for access to federal information and systems with the need to protect and adequately mitigate risk."}, {"source_id": "ia-8.2_gdn", "span_text": "Acceptance of only NIST-compliant external authenticators applies to organizational systems that are accessible to the public (e.g., public-facing websites). External authenticators are issued by nonfederal government entities and are compliant with [SP 800-63B](#e59c5a7c-8b1f-49ca-8de0-6ee0882180ce) . Approved external authenticators meet or exceed the minimum Federal Government-wide technical, security, privacy, and organizational maturity requirements. Meeting or exceeding Federal requirements allows Federal Government relying parties to trust external authenticators in connection with an authentication transaction at a specified authenticator assurance level."}, {"source_id": "ia-8.2_smt", "span_text": "(a) Accept only external authenticators that are NIST-compliant; and (b) Document and maintain a list of accepted external authenticators."}, {"source_id": "ia-8.2_smt.a", "span_text": "Accept only external authenticators that are NIST-compliant; and"}, {"source_id": "ia-8.2_smt.b", "span_text": "Document and maintain a list of accepted external authenticators."}], "status": "OK", "odp_required_list": [], "ask_list": [], "primary_citation": "ia-8_gdn", "all_citations": "ia-8_gdn, ia-8.2_gdn, ia-8.2_smt, ia-8.2_smt.a, ia-8.2_smt.b", "contract_mode": "generative_rag_baseline", "debug": {"query_plan": {"original_query": "How should organizations handle identification and authentication of non-organizational users accessing federal systems?", "rewrites": ["What are the best practices for identifying and authenticating external users in federal systems?", "How can organizations securely manage the identification and authentication of non-employee users accessing federal IT systems?", "What methodologies do security experts recommend for verifying the identity of external users accessing federal systems?"]}, "retrieval_meta": {"base_margin_ratio": 0.06791071290306912, "base_top1": "IA-8", "base_top2": "IA-2", "bm25_top1": null, "dense_top1": null, "final_margin_ratio": 0.062088608741760254, "final_top1": "IA-8", "n_docs": 32, "num_variants": 4, "ranked_controls": ["IA-8", "IA-2", "AC-14", "IA-2(2)", "IA-8(2)", "AC-6(6)", "IA-1", "IA-2(1)", "IA-10", "IA-3", "IA-13", "IA-9", "IA-12(6)", "AC-3(14)", "PL-4", "AC-20", "AC-6(2)", "PL-4(1)", "IA-5(9)", "AC-11", "AC-20(3)", "IA-5(8)", "IA-12", "IA-2(5)", "SA-4(10)", "IA-5(10)", "SI-4(20)", "IA-8(4)", "IA-5", "AC-20(1)", "SC-2(1)", "IA-3(4)", "CA-2(3)", "IA-11", "CA-6", "AC-2", "IA-4(5)", "AU-16", "IA-8(6)", "AC-24(2)", "AC-16(4)", "AC-8", "SI-18", "CA-6(2)", "AU-6(9)", "IR-2", "IA-7", "AC-6(10)", "PT-8", "SA-9(4)"], "rerank_alpha": 0.65, "rerank_applied": true, "rerank_apply_min_margin_ratio": 0.15, "rerank_effective_apply_min_margin_ratio": 0.1, "rerank_margin_ratio": 0.062088608741760254, "rerank_skip_min_base_margin_ratio": 0.1, "rerank_skip_require_top1_agreement": false, "rerank_top1": "IA-8", "reranker_called": true, "selected_clause_ids_by_control": {"AC-14": ["ac-14_gdn", "ac-14_smt", "ac-14_smt.a", "ac-14_smt.b"], "AC-6(6)": ["ac-6.6_gdn", "ac-6.6_smt"], "IA-