{"question": "What measures should be implemented to monitor and review physical access logs and respond to security incidents in facilities housing systems?", "framework_version": "rev5", "answer_text": "Monitor physical access to the facility where the system resides using physical intrusion alarms and surveillance equipment, and review physical access logs for suspicious activity, anomalous events, or potential threats.", "answer_text_with_citations": "Monitor physical access to the facility where the system resides using physical intrusion alarms and surveillance equipment, and review physical access logs for suspicious activity, anomalous events, or potential threats.

Citations: pe-6.1_smt, pe-6_smt.b, pe-6_gdn (NIST SP 800-53 Rev. 5)", "evidence_spans": [{"source_id": "pe-6.1_smt", "span_text": "Monitor physical access to the facility where the system resides using physical intrusion alarms and surveillance equipment."}, {"source_id": "pe-6_smt.b", "span_text": "Review physical access logs {{ insert: param, pe-06_odp.01 }} and upon occurrence of {{ insert: param, pe-06_odp.02 }} ; and"}, {"source_id": "pe-6_gdn", "span_text": "Physical access monitoring includes publicly accessible areas within organizational facilities. Examples of physical access monitoring include the employment of guards, video surveillance equipment (i.e., cameras), and sensor devices. Reviewing physical access logs can help identify suspicious activity, anomalous events, or potential threats. The reviews can be supported by audit logging controls, such as [AU-2](#au-2) , if the access logs are part of an automated system. Organizational incident response capabilities include investigations of physical security incidents and responses to the incidents. Incidents include security violations or suspicious physical access activities. Suspicious physical access activities include accesses outside of normal work hours, repeated accesses to areas not normally accessed, accesses for unusual lengths of time, and out-of-sequence accesses."}], "status": "OK", "odp_required_list": [], "ask_list": [], "primary_citation": "pe-6.1_smt", "all_citations": "pe-6.1_smt, pe-6_smt.b, pe-6_gdn", "contract_mode": "generative_rag_baseline", "debug": {"query_plan": {"original_query": "What measures should be implemented to monitor and review physical access logs and respond to security incidents in facilities housing systems?", "rewrites": ["How can we ensure effective monitoring and review of physical access logs and timely response to security incidents in facility environments?", "What technical controls are necessary for the surveillance and examination of physical access records and the prompt handling of security breaches in building settings?", "Can you outline the best practices for keeping track of physical access logs and addressing security events in locations that house IT systems?"]}, "retrieval_meta": {"base_margin_ratio": 0.04332849331554773, "base_top1": "PE-6", "base_top2": "PE-3", "bm25_top1": null, "dense_top1": null, "final_margin_ratio": 0.1424494981765747, "final_top1": "PE-6", "n_docs": 44, "num_variants": 4, "ranked_controls": ["PE-6", "PE-3", "PE-6(4)", "PE-6(1)", "PE-3(1)", "AU-6(6)", "PE-2", "SC-7(14)", "PE-4", "PE-1", "AC-3", "AU-6", "IR-4", "AT-3(2)", "RA-5(8)", "CM-5(1)", "PE-5", "CA-8(3)", "PE-6(2)", "AU-2", "PE-3(3)", "CM-2(7)", "AC-17(1)", "CA-7", "PE-3(8)", "SI-4", "PS-5", "AC-1", "IR-5", "CP-6(3)", "CA-7(4)", "PE-2(1)", "AC-25", "AU-12(3)", "RA-6", "IR-4(9)", "IR-4(14)", "PE-18", "CM-5", "PE-13(1)", "AU-1", "SA-8(22)", "PM-4", "PE-3(2)", "MA-2", "AC-6(1)", "AU-9(4)", "PE-13(4)", "AU-4(1)", "PM-6"], "rerank_alpha": 0.65, "rerank_applied": true, "rerank_apply_min_margin_ratio": 0.15, "rerank_effective_apply_min_margin_ratio": 0.1, "rerank_margin_ratio": 0.1424494981765747, "rerank_skip_min_base_margin_ratio": 0.1, "rerank_skip_require_top1_agreement": false, "rerank_top1": "PE-6", "reranker_called": true, "selected_clause_ids_by_control": {"AC-3": ["ac-3_gdn", "ac-3_smt"], "AU-6": ["au-6_gdn", "au-6_smt.c", "au-6_smt", "au-6_smt.b", "au-6_smt.a"], "AU-6(6)": ["au-6.6_smt", "au-6.6_gdn"], "PE-1": ["pe-1_smt.c", "pe-1_gdn", "pe-1_smt.a.2"], "PE-2": ["pe-2_smt", "pe-2_smt.c", "pe-2_gdn", "pe-2_smt.b", "pe-2_smt.a", "pe-2_smt.d"], "PE-3": ["pe-3_smt.b", "pe-3_smt", "pe-3_gdn", "pe-3_smt.c", "pe-3_smt.e", "pe-3_smt.a.1", "pe-3_smt.a", "pe-3_smt.a.2", "pe-3_smt.f", "pe-3_smt.g", "pe-3_smt.d"], "PE-3(1)": ["pe-3.1_gdn", "pe-3.1_smt"], "PE-4": ["pe-4_smt", "pe-4_gdn"], "PE-6": ["pe-6_gdn", "pe-6_smt", "pe-6_smt.a", "pe-6_smt.b", "pe-6_smt.c"], "PE-6(1)": ["pe-6.1_smt", "pe-6.1_gdn"], "PE-6(4)": ["pe-6.4_smt", "pe-6.4