{"question": "When and how must individuals be screened before authorizing or maintaining access to organizational systems?", "framework_version": "rev5", "answer_text": "Individuals must be screened prior to authorizing access to the system. The screening should be conducted in accordance with applicable laws, executive orders, directives, regulations, policies, standards, guidelines, and specific criteria established for the risk designations of assigned positions.", "answer_text_with_citations": "Individuals must be screened prior to authorizing access to the system. The screening should be conducted in accordance with applicable laws, executive orders, directives, regulations, policies, standards, guidelines, and specific criteria established for the risk designations of assigned positions.

Citations: ps-3_gdn (NIST SP 800-53 Rev. 5)", "evidence_spans": [{"source_id": "ps-3_gdn", "span_text": "Personnel screening and rescreening activities reflect applicable laws, executive orders, directives, regulations, policies, standards, guidelines, and specific criteria established for the risk designations of assigned positions. Examples of personnel screening include background investigations and agency checks. Organizations may define different rescreening conditions and frequencies for personnel accessing systems based on types of information processed, stored, or transmitted by the systems."}], "status": "OK", "odp_required_list": [], "ask_list": [], "primary_citation": "ps-3_gdn", "all_citations": "ps-3_gdn", "contract_mode": "generative_rag_baseline", "debug": {"query_plan": {"original_query": "When and how must individuals be screened before authorizing or maintaining access to organizational systems?", "rewrites": ["When and what methods must be used to screen individuals before granting them access to organizational systems?", "What are the required screening procedures for individuals before they are authorized to access organizational systems?", "Screening protocols for individuals prior to accessing organizational systems, what are they?"]}, "retrieval_meta": {"base_margin_ratio": 0.13292414212356582, "base_top1": "PS-3", "base_top2": "AC-20", "bm25_top1": null, "dense_top1": null, "final_margin_ratio": 0.13292414212356582, "final_top1": "PS-3", "n_docs": 47, "num_variants": 4, "ranked_controls": ["PS-3", "AC-20", "PS-6", "AC-2(13)", "AC-8", "AC-3(14)", "IA-2", "SA-21", "CA-6", "CM-3(2)", "PM-10", "AC-3(9)", "AC-20(1)", "MA-5(1)", "CM-2(7)", "AC-14", "IA-2(5)", "SI-18(4)", "PL-4", "AC-18(4)", "SA-9(4)", "MA-5", "CP-2(8)", "IA-8", "PE-3", "AC-16(2)", "CA-2(1)", "MA-5(3)", "PS-3(4)", "AC-3(7)", "AT-3", "CA-1", "SA-9(7)", "CA-2(2)", "IA-4(5)", "SA-4(9)", "PE-2", "AC-20(3)", "AC-1", "AC-6(6)", "PS-1", "MA-5(4)", "AU-16", "PT-5(1)", "AC-6(7)", "CM-7(1)",